Changes to UGREEN's DXP2800 GT driver (ugreen-opensource/kernel-6.12, drivers/ugreen/ug_201x.c and
leds-sio-201x.c at commit 0e4d73a6893d2aaa9772345c85bcccb3798784c1), applied by DKMS before building.
This file is a modification of GPL-2.0 code, so it is GPL-2.0-only, unlike the rest of this repository (MIT).

- /proc/it86/fan and startup are root-only (0600) and temp read-only (0444); UGREEN made them writable by anyone,
  so any local account could stop the fans or change the power-on-after-power-fail setting.
- Writes to fan and startup reject an empty write, which read the byte before their buffer.
- The proc files are opened with single_open, so they're released with single_release; seq_release leaked a little
  memory on every open.
- remove() no longer removes a "version" entry that is never created.
- LEDs: any brightness above 0 turns the LED on (UGREEN treated only 1 as on, so the kernel's own triggers, which
  write the maximum, could switch an LED off but never back on); led_set_on_off's bounds check is fixed.

